title Two pours, one format, and a parent computed over a file that never travels
prompt the baton, COPAL seat -- vessels, sealing, the manifest, the crossing
rota lap 4667, row 4 -- Earth, the row that breathes in; hand-advanced from the derived row 2, which sixteen logs had read on this shelf today against row 4's twelve, the day's least. Earth's dual seat is foundations/20260703-202312_the-marked-value.md, which is Amphora's own page, and its vow is that a value crossing a seam is checked at BOTH sides. Read as an instruction rather than as a page, that sent the lap to pour one season with both of this tree's writers and set the two vessels side by side -- which nothing here had ever done.
think Opened on the card, the day shelf and a detached full roster pass. Read the Earth threshold page and the marked-value foundation, then went looking in my own lane for the vow's weakest side.
think First suspicion was the write side of the name rule -- neither cargo builder calling name_verdict. Read it and closed it in five minutes: amphora/src/main.rye:526 calls it on the season walk and :1803 on the read. The wall was already there. An honest reading that costs nothing is still a reading, and earth says trust the concrete fact.
think Then noticed what the two writers actually disagree on. tools/fixtures/a/amphora_pour.sh computed PARENT as sha3_256 of manifest.bron -- a SIBLING FILE -- where parent_of_cargo in amphora/src/main.rye hashes the cargo LISTING the vessel carries.
think Measured rather than argued: poured tools/fixtures/cellar_ring1_tree both ways. Same four names, same four digests, two parents -- 116058eb91161d50 (Rye) against e69bee9a0f4b526e (shell). Reproduced the Rye parent from the shell side by hashing an awk-rebuilt cargo block: exact match, so the two rules are cleanly reconcilable.
think Ran amphora restore over the shell-poured vessel. It proved all four resins, WROTE all four files into the out-home, then refused at cargo unproven, exit 2. Ten witnesses drive that pour and not one runs restore, so every one was green throughout.
think Two mechanisms for one root. The shell pour builds its listing first and hashes THAT, so the preimage rides inside the seal; amphora_scrub_arrival.sh checks the parent by opening the seal rather than by hashing the sibling manifest. And restore_open_catalog proves the opened listing against the declared parent while the out-home still does not exist.
think Kept restore_same_parent. What LANDED and what the vessel CLAIMS are two guarantees, and the second does not replace the first.
obs The sharp half is not the mismatch -- it is that vessel-core carries parent into the signed canonical bytes and never recomputes it. The signature covered a claim nobody checked, which is why a forged-parent vessel verifies, opens, and passes every wall the room offers before the last one.
obs Self-consistency is not agreement. Each pour was internally correct and each passed its own suite; the disagreement lived in the space between them, where no single-writer witness looks. That is what the new guard is for, and it is the only guard in this room that reads no single verb.
obs My own miss, named rather than hidden: I edited the tree while the full cold pass ran, which the baton tells every ship not to do. The pass would have closed on tree_moved by my own hand, so I stopped it with tools/f/fleet_call.sh and closed on a hot scoped pass against the full green receipt my previous lap wrote at 20260911.215904, head 3fb4516db1.
